<p style="font-size:20px !important;font-weight:700;color:#0f172a !important;margin:0 0 12px;line-height:1.4;">Should you buy a house in Florida in 2026?</p>
<p style="font-size:18px;line-height:1.7;color:#374151;margin:0;"><strong style="color:#0f172a;">Yes, if you're planning to stay 7-10 years and can afford the full monthly cost.</strong> Florida's housing market has cooled from the pandemic frenzy but remains expensive. Median home price sits at $415,000, inventory has doubled to 4.6 months, and mortgage rates hover near 6%. The biggest wild card? <a href="/florida-homeowners-insurance-guide/" style="color:#0f172a !important;text-decoration:underline;">Insurance costs</a> that can add $400-$600/month to your payment. Across <a href="/tampa/" style="color:#0f172a !important;text-decoration:underline;">Tampa Bay</a>, homes under $425K with new roofs are still moving in 25-30 days.</p>
