<h3 style="color:#0f172a;font-size:20px;font-weight:700;line-height:1.3;margin-top:32px;margin-bottom:12px;">Should I buy a condo in Florida?</h3>

<p style="font-size:18px;line-height:1.8;color:#374151;margin-bottom:20px;"><strong style="color:#0f172a;">Proceed with caution.</strong> Condos face unique 2026 challenges. On the plus side: lower entry price ($280K-$350K median), 9+ month inventory gives you negotiating power, and low maintenance lifestyle. On the downside: post-Surfside safety laws mean special assessments of $20K-$100K+, HOA fees rising (many up 30-50% since 2022), harder to finance (lenders require more reserves), and insurance crisis is worse for older buildings. Your best bet is newer condos built 2015+ with healthy reserves. Avoid pre-1980 coastal high-rises.</p>

